# 3. Make local editing and saving immediate

[Organization and execution order](record:r_0PCR2DTXNGTQGBE6RBWR0ECTXW). Targets are in [benchmarks](record:r_7CWV5KN1695FW2KNPGW5X19PJ7); interaction coverage is in [workflows](record:r_33DFSQHTZFRCM758HHPN3KRWNA).

**Coordination:** the earlier sync/history/database-lock/Karma delegation is historical. Inspect the current working tree before changing shared mutation/history/transaction/effect paths; do not assume an old agent is still active or that its work is complete. P94 remains unresolved without its own cause/result receipt. Preserve unrelated changes and keep backend correctness distinct from measured interface responsiveness.

Backend correctness fixes are not substitutes for Stage A's latency proof, and “saving is another agent's task” does not excuse a frozen interface. Keep immediate echo and unrelated input independent of required durable work, measure contention from normal sync/history/Karma activity and preserve truthful save/effect status. General feature/semantic repairs beyond these dependencies stay outside this performance queue.

Continue from the remaining title/description echo and save delays. Borrowed editor reads/splicing, incremental recovery and bounded background checkpoint encoding are complete; their earlier evidence is in 00. Canonical text/checkpoint, shared Fact invalidation, retained description and direct save-reply ownership reductions are now implemented source, with verification pending in Overhaul.md. Necessary common-text scans, canonical document/history processing and inline ordinary Cell request handling still have costs; their existence alone does not establish a safe removal or request-order change. Reuse the completed P102 attribution and investigate a specific remaining dependency before changing its boundary. Profile-save JSON already has a background writer and is separate.

Preserve immediate draft text, durable recovery, canonical local commit, publication and remote sync as distinct states. Local input must not wait for network acknowledgement. Do not replace durability with a longer debounce alone. Reuse the existing Record mutation, Loro and storage families. Every write experiment must test actual file-backed reopen/recovery, not only an in-memory database. Source anchors: native/record_binding.rs, record_view.rs, description.rs, protein_area; native/cell_bridge.rs; crates/transport/src/session.rs; engine/record_change.rs and store/record_docs.rs.

**Implemented, verification pending:** the legacy RecordEditor save path now routes admitted replies directly, retires stale owner routes, borrows reply details and avoids identical feedback writes. Canonical TextBinding persistence is separate and unchanged by this reduction. EDIT-1E in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md) owns draft, error, lifecycle and complete-cost verification; do not reopen this as a missing implementation.

**Implemented, verification pending:** queued Fact invalidations now share one bounded current-state refresh wave in the transport used by native, mobile and remote clients. Overhaul.md’s REFRESH-VERIFY owns the remaining check. This reduces repeated reads; it does not merge writes, bypass required reactions or complete P121’s conditional slow-request isolation. Do not reimplement the queued-notification reduction. The same shared path now derives canonical Record scope once per wave, lazily and without set allocation for a one-Record burst. Identical query aliases converge on one row allocation and reuse comparisons through weak per-wave identities. The original conservative invalidation, publication, history and access rules remain; REFRESH-VERIFY owns equivalence, alias lifecycle and full-cost verification.

**Implemented, verification pending:** workspace saving reserves its existing pending slot before full recovery capture, avoiding discarded captures when storage is busy. Atomic work metadata and single slug-register writes are implemented under P120. WORKSPACE-STORAGE-VERIFY and WORK-PROPERTY-VERIFY in Overhaul.md own their checks. Local sync provenance/root reads and collision insertion now share one fresh context statement and borrowed operation path; SYNC-LOG-VERIFY retains validation. No requests, history entries or durability boundaries are batched. Neither is a missing worker implementation or evidence that canonical text-save latency is solved.

**Continue through these Records:**

- [P116 — Amortize one stream of local edit commits without delaying feedback.](record:r_7W7WPY7YF5B16QZ47SKY0QR6NH)
- [P117 — Verify bounded canonical checkpoint admission.](record:r_7HD3G5KF1QDXZ5Y766H0WVQ357)
- [P137 — Verify canonical field-text sharing.](record:r_2QC1RKFFQJ09XEE7EP15KJW6E1)
- [P94 — Identify the cause of the database-locked toast.](record:r_576VQH1YFK5VPC5GM9024714EW)
- [P138 — Shorten the engine-wide access gate without weakening operation validity.](record:r_6T8CDPK9MX8J93FHM5Q5JE1TA4)
- [P139 — Remove unnecessary post-commit reaction waiting from local save feedback.](record:r_6PB6GYZ446CWCNNVS8JENYY414)
- [P121 — Prevent a slow Cell request from delaying unrelated local edit service.](record:r_5E9VPP06MSXAM46V1MNA6T163P)
- [P119 — Verify retained description blocks and deferred Raw preview.](record:r_2C28QTRHSFACYE70MCH58SRPYS)
- [P120 — Verify single final work projections and slug-register writes.](record:r_5FDXR01ABJBD6FW36MWABGMPZQ)
} r_0BZMR3P9CJ1WPW82SG9AX5WPVA

P116 — Amortize one stream of local edit commits without delaying feedback. (
    @park-p116: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-03-local-edits-and-storage: 13,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_7W7WPY7YF5B16QZ47SKY0QR6NH
**Current workflow:** [Development cycle](record:r_043BC6V4K9R3X6E9E4TZP3P6J0). **Resume state:** [Current checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y).

**Context:** [Source chapter](record:r_0BZMR3P9CJ1WPW82SG9AX5WPVA); [execution queue](record:r_1FMCTGVHF35B6D0T70JEQAMYDW). **Stage:** A1 · coordinate.


**Why:** one draft/canonical transaction per character or view can multiply durable I/O and backend effects. **Scope:** use P102's write counts to batch compatible pending changes for one local document within a bounded latency window, preserving individual operation IDs, ordering, conflict and undo/history semantics. A canonical transaction may absorb recovery work only if it provides the same recoverability. Keep local echo immediate and explicit save/close/flush as real barriers; do not merge distinct commands, assertions, counter deltas or auditable side effects merely because they are adjacent. **Verify:** concurrent views, typing while a write is blocked, rapid edits then close, failure/replay and bounded journal age. Include p95/p99 durability and effects, not just commits/second. **Needs:** the completed incremental recovery path (00) and honest status boundaries.

**Current evidence/selection:** P150's four-run private follow-up records exactly 15 WAL sync calls during three edits (five per edit), plus one/two negligible directory sync calls. The slow run spends 609.55 ms in these nonoverlapping calls; the other runs spend 53.06–64.35 ms. Reuse this trace and the draft/canonical/history counters to map each required boundary before selecting a reduction. A syscall count is not independently a transaction count. Prefer folding genuinely redundant recovery/cleanup work into an already necessary valid transaction when it preserves the exact draft generation and recovery semantics; bounded batching must help ordinary typing or a named burst workload rather than merely delaying local saves. Keep every required per-query history entry, error, cancellation and publication guarantee. Full optimized/physical impact remains unproved.

**Ownership traced:** native record_binding dispatch waits until its recovery metadata contains the operation ID. Canonical commit persists an actor-scoped exact-payload receipt, and its acknowledgement dirties the journal again alongside the two affected-query history writes. An unconditional recovery-write skip or delayed cleanup would therefore change recovery/replay behavior; receipt ID alone is insufficient without actor, payload, source/generation and stale-save handling. These source constraints retain P116 as open. Short debounce alone does not remove the five boundaries of ordinary sequential edits. P137's selected field-text sharing is now implemented and verification-only; do not reopen it as the next coding step. Workspace capture admission and atomic work-metadata projection are also implemented, but neither combines the separate canonical text/recovery/history transactions discussed here.
} r_7W7WPY7YF5B16QZ47SKY0QR6NH

