) { r_7HD3G5KF1QDXZ5Y766H0WVQ357
**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** The canonical write transaction asks whether the CRDT tail reaches the checkpoint threshold in one bounded query, using that same transaction and the newly appended operation. Remote persistence also reads only the ownership column at its original fresh-read boundary instead of loading a second full Record. Commit/history/authorization semantics are unchanged.

**Still to verify:** Check below/at/above threshold, absent checkpoints, imported and duplicate operations, atom-triggered checkpoints, rollback, replay and reopen. Attribute transaction query/hold time and complete acknowledgement under contention.

**Why:** A yes/no checkpoint decision should not count the entire tail or acquire a second query result unnecessarily.

**Current instruction:** source changes only. Do not run checks, compile, measure, ship or restart from this Record. Use [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md#remaining-acceptance-obligations) and [the checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y); verification resumes only when authorized. Quantity remains zero because implementation is not a performance pass.
} r_7HD3G5KF1QDXZ5Y766H0WVQ357

