P119 — Verify retained description blocks and deferred Raw preview. (
    @park-p119: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-03-local-edits-and-storage: 51,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_2C28QTRHSFACYE70MCH58SRPYS
**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** The shared description renderer retains parsed block views, reuses unchanged prefixes/suffixes and matching middle blocks, and updates compatible paragraph spans and ordinary code-block text in place. Images, diagrams, shader state and live subscribed transclusions retain their existing owners. Changed render structure rebuilds only its affected block. The ordinary parser still reads the complete source so reference definitions, fences and list syntax can affect other blocks correctly.

Raw editing no longer parses or rebuilds its hidden preview. Pretty/Split synchronizes the latest editor text before showing it. Persistence, local text/undo and live subscription/permission processing remain independent. Source/context/ancestry changes invalidate reuse. One-shot source transclusions retain their existing refresh boundary; view-limit and refused-subscription fallbacks remain retryable on a later edit rather than being retained as permanent content. Child ordering uses the shared retained-children family and preserves independently owned children.

**Still to verify:** paragraph and plain-code edits, insertion/deletion and duplicate blocks; cross-block syntax and links; image/diagram/shader lifetimes; Raw/Pretty/Split transitions after many edits; selection/focus/scroll; scope changes, live permission removal, exhausted quotas, late async results and close/reopen. Compare description-markup-blocks-retained/patched/rebuilt, parsed source bytes, complete input/preview time, work-to-complete and retained memory in small/large documents. Full parsing and one retained parsed representation still cost CPU/memory; no measured saving is claimed.

**Why:** editing one paragraph should not recreate unrelated controls, redraw already prepared media or restart their subscriptions. Hidden preview work should not delay Raw typing. No execution is authorized in the current source-only phase.

} r_2C28QTRHSFACYE70MCH58SRPYS

