P120 — Verify single final work projections and slug-register writes. (
    @park-p120: 0,
    is #task,
    #park-performance-task,
    #park-stage-a1,
    #part-of @park-dev-03-local-edits-and-storage: 55,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_5FDXR01ABJBD6FW36MWABGMPZQ
**Status — implemented, verification pending (2026-11-15).** Complete WorkMetadata requests now prepare log matching once, stage accepted fields in memory and write one validated final work projection in their existing transaction. Individual registers, sync/history/Fact order, receipts, authority, rollback and durable acknowledgements remain. The duplicate identical register upsert after slug arbitration is removed. Streaming value-size checks and borrowed occurrence decoding avoid discarded encoded/JSON copies. Imported legacy work extensions also restore authoritative scalar/log registers into one validated final projection, retaining the same immediate transaction boundary. The 2026-11-16 continuation extends final log projection to each Timer request, keeping all individual registers/sync/history and one final validation before commit. No-op requests gain no projection work. Complete replacements reuse admitted input-subtree validation; final merged state remains validated. Shared parsed endpoint/range handling, validation-only log consumption and borrowed single-log validation are implemented under WORK-VALIDATION-VERIFY; they are no longer coding TODOs.

**Still to verify:** WORK-PROPERTY-VERIFY in [Overhaul.md](Overhaul.md#remaining-acceptance-obligations) covers exact duplicate/order/rank behavior, final-state limits, failure/replay/reopen, individual/remote operations, slug arbitration, statement counts and complete resource/latency cost. Equal content is not a reason to discard a newer collaborative operation. Shared query-result suppression is a separate implemented reduction under REFRESH-VERIFY.

**Why:** one atomic metadata edit should not repeatedly read, validate, encode and write its whole extension; one accepted slug register needs one upsert. This removes concrete redundant preparation/statements without merging separate commands or changing save acknowledgement. No measured gain is claimed.

**Current instruction:** source changes only. Do not compile, execute SQL, test, measure, ship or restart. Quantity stays zero until the remaining verification is complete.
} r_5FDXR01ABJBD6FW36MWABGMPZQ

